We have nine Alpha's running RedHat Linux, some of them 4.2, some 5.0.
There are no major problems with running Linux on these machines. Two
issues that you might worry about are: 1. The NFS performance. The
implementation of the NFS in the 2.0.xx kernels is very slow. In addition
the default is set for a pentium class machine which is not at all
adequate for an Alpha machine. At least you need to mount the NFS filesystems
with the options rsize=8192,wsize=8192 which will aleviate some of the
probem. The NFS code is expected to be greatly improved in the 2.2 kernel.
2. The compilers. gcc and g77 generates codes that are much much slower
than DEC compilers. If you do any numerical applications, get DU.

Xiaoguang Zhang

