olli.ohlsson@usa.net wrote:
> 
> Hi, I just installed complete RedHat 5.0 to my noname box.
> After long fight with X-windows configurator finally got
> it working, but now the mouse does not function. How to
> set up the mouse? I have AT model of noname board and have
> to use serial port for it.
> 

You need to take the connector off the motherboard end and reconfigure
it. The pinouts are not the same as a PC. The pinouts are given in Table
17 of the OEM Design Guide for the AXPpci33. They are as follows(taken
from my manual)

Pin #	Function
1	DCD
2	Serial Out
3	Ground
4	RTS
5	RI
6	Serial In
7	DTR
8	DSR
9	CTS
10	(No pin)

For a PC 9 pin D connector they are:

1	DCD
2	RXD
3	TXD
4	DTR
5	Ground
6	DSR
7	RTS
8	CTS
9	RI

Therefore, disconnect the black connector fromthe ribbon cable, seperate
all the individual wires, and wire it up with the correct signals.

It was a great source of frustration for me when I first got my Alpha
running, then I relized the pinouts weren't the same. After I changed
the cable my mouse worked just fine. If you have any more specific
questions, feel free to email me. Good luck.



