This is not fully correct. There are some PCs which have this pinout.=20
The whole thing is a matter of in which direction you count the pins.

Some Manufacturers do it this way:

(01) (03) (05) (07) (09)
(02) (04) (06) (08) (10)

other do:

(01) (02) (03) (04) (05)
(06) (07) (08) (09) (10)


Normally on both Pin 2 =3D RxD, 3 =3D TxD, 5 =3D GND. But it seems =
Digital used
the one pinout, but the other counting. They have RxD on 6, TxD on 2 and
GND on 3. If you compare the tho diagrams above, you will find, that
Pin 2 =3D RxD is =3D=3D Pin 6 =3D RxD on the other and so on. So if you =
search a=20
bit, you may found correct connectors.


