If you can scare up two 9 pin connectors from older machines, the wires on
them pretty much go straight in. It's kinda strange to explain but if you
saw one you would know exactly what I mean. I think there may have been an
error in some edition of the book because the one that I made according to
the book didn't work the first time. 

Basically, hook the red striped wire to pin 1, the next one to pin 6
(bottom row between 1 and 2), and continue the whole way.

djweis

