One problem I had was that the kernel comes up and fails to autosense
the BNC (10base2) port. This is a problem with the Tulip driver, which
should have been fixed in a later version. I was not able to get this
corrected even after building withg the latest tulip driver, but the
kernel I built has some problems. Since I have a 10baseT to 10base2 hub,
I am using the 10baseT port. Works fine on the AUI port also. My
suggestion, is that if you are trying to use BNC, check to see if the
kernel detects it on boot. The Tulip driver contains some code to force
sensing of the BNC port. 
