> I have problems running gperf on the alpha. Compiling egcs asks for it
> For now I just run gprf on a 586 mounting the alpha disk but this is
> not the most desired solution.

Egcs will try to run gperf if c-gperf.h is out of date with respect to 
c-parse.gperf.  In snapshots and distributions this normally is not the case 
- however, due to the way snapshots are built, the timestamps sometimes might 
be out of order.  Try `touch'ing c-gperf.h and continue `make bootstrap' to 
see if this helps.

Groeten,

