Steven N. Hirsch wrote:

[...]
 
> >Please note that this implies that you will have to use
> >a qt library compiled with egcs, and libstdc++-2.8.x.
> 
> For my own edification, why should it matter what compiler is used to
> build the qt library so long as it's linked against a current glibc?
> 
> Steve

As I don't know too much about the internals of compilers,
just a vague answer: The way C++ symbols are mapped to C
symbols (name unmangling(?)) has changed somwhere between
gcc-2.7 and egcs (I don't know anything about gcc-2.8 for sure,
but I guess it is compatible to egcs). This results in a 
number of unresolved symbols, if you try to link a egcs
compiled program against a gcc-2.7 compiled library and vice
versa. 

Hope this was not too wrong ;-)

