install the most minimal system you could, and install the rest of the
packages you want by hand from there on.  Now, I don't know what
constitutes a 'most minimal system' with Red Hat Linux, but now that I
have everything installed, I have had no problems (even while running
development kernels and a 3.3.2 X server with the rest of the X setup
