I am also using the Tekram DC390F (Symbios 875) on an SX164 with Linux 
and it works fine.  I am using the SRM (OpenVMS/Digital Unix) console
which recognizes the disks on the card and allows me to boot from the
card.  It is very fast and I have never had any problems on a running
system with the card or a drive attached to it.

However, I cannot recommend that you get this card for use with the
alpha, as it hangs while trying to identify any external devices.
This is at the console when doing ``show dev'' or when trying to boot
from a disk attached to the card.  I imagine this has to do with the
cards automatic termination (which works great on Intel hardware).  I
have not yet tried putting the card in an Intel box and disabling
automatic termination.  It was easier to just put a Symbios 825 based
card in the alpha and use that to attach external devices (compare the
price of an active 68 pin terminator to the price of a low end PCI
SCSI card).

--
Jeff Lessem.



