Michael Champigny wrote:

> What does this message mean and can anyone give me a *detailed* walk through
> of how you got Linux installed on this beast.

Michael: Here are the notes from when we went through this with an XL300 from
two weeks ago.  Hope it helps!

Bruce Allen

Set up an operating system choice on Alpha BIOS

1.  dd if=milo/images/xl.img of=/dev/fd0

2. Got the latest version of MILO built with 2.0.30
 and copied on the disk in step 1.

3.  Built RAMDISK on a separate floppy as given in the redhat
 manual (pp 48).

4. On milo prompt booted the kernel cdrom:/kernels/xlt.img
 xl.img did not work.

-----------------------------------------------------------------

1. reset the machine
2. choose setup by pressing function key F2 at the OS load screen
 system waits for 5secs or goes into default loading of NT.
3. Alphabios set up screen  go to  UTILITIES
 and select  OS selection setup
4. Choose New (insert key)
5. set the boot name to Linux<TAB>
 set boot file to A: <TAB>  linload.exe <TAB>
 set  the OS Path to Disk 0, Partition 1 <TAB> \
 Leave OS Options blank
  (You  can use the up and down cursor keys to select some options)
6. Save changes made by hitting the F10 key and confirm when the
 window pops up.

7. Hit ESC twice to get to the OS load screen

8. Insert the MILO disk and then select Linux and hit <enter>


9. Wait for the MILO prompt. Insert the Linux CDROM.
 Remove the MILO floppy.  Insert the RAMDISK floppy.

10. At MILO prompt key in ..
 boot -t iso9660 sr0:kernels/xlt.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
prompt_ramdisk=1

11. The system prompts for the RAMDISK. Make sure the RAMDISK is in the floppy
drive
 and hit enter.

12. Wait for the Welcome to RedHat screen


 Screens

13. Select the monitor (color or not).

14. Welcome message. Hit enter.

15. Select Keyboard (us)

16. Installation method  (Local CDROM)

17. Insert your CDROM and hit enter.

18. Installation path (install)

19. Partition disks (edit)

20. fdisk program presents a prompt:


 hit 'p' for viewing the partition table.
  There should be 5 partitions.
 hit 'd' <enter> 1 <enter>
  This will delete the first partition.
 Delete the remaining partitions as above.
 Hit 'p' to make sure that all the partitions are deleted.
 hit 'n' for making a new partition.
 hit 'p'  to select primary partition.
 hit 1 to indicate the first partition.
 first cylinder = 1 <enter> Last cylinder = 288 <enter>


 Hit 'n' again to create partition number 2.
 hit 'p'  to select primary partition.
 hit 2 to indicate the 2nd partition.
 first cylinder = 289 <enter> Last cylinder = +256 <enter>

 Hit 'n' again to create partition number 3.
 hit 'p'  to select primary partition.
 hit 3 to indicate the 3rd partition.
 first cylinder = 546 <enter> Last cylinder = +150 <enter>


 Hit 'n' again to create partition number 4.
 hit 'p'  to select primary partition.
 hit 4 to indicate the 4th partition.
 first cylinder = 697 <enter> Last cylinder = 1009 <enter>

 Hit 't' to change the patition type.
 hit '1'
 hit 82

 hit 'a' to make a partition bootable
 hit '2' to make the 2nd partition bootable.
 hit 'w' to save and exit.

 You are back to the 'Partition disk screen'


21. select done

22. Active Swap Space screen: select  <ok> by hitting <TAB> twice.

23. Select Root Partition screen: select /dev/sda2 <enter>

24. partition Disk screen: move to /dev/sda3 <enter>  and label the mount point
as /usr
 and select ok and <enter>

25.  Back to previous screen: move to /dev/sda4 and <enter>
 label mount point as /home <enter>

26. Back to previous screen:
 Select NFS Setup

 IP address : xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx
 Netmask    : 255.255.255.0
 default gateway:  xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx
 primary nameserver: xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx

 hit <enter>

27. Configure Network screen:
 domain name:   xxx.xxx.xxx.edu
 host name:  xxx.xxx.xxx.edu
 secondary nameserver (IP) xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx

28. edit network mount point
 nfs server: chandra.phys.uwm.edu
 NFS path  : /home
 mount point: /linuxhome
 <enter>

 edit network mount point
 nfs server: dirac.phys.uwm.edu
 NFS path  :  /home
 mount point: /sunhome
 select ok and <enter>

 edit network mount point
 nfs server: pauli.phys.uwm.edu
 NFS path  :  /usr/users
 mount point: /paulihome
 select ok and <enter>

29: Format partitions:
 Select all the partitions with a <space>.
 check for bad blocks with <space>
 select ok and <enter>

30: Components to install:

 C Development
 Development libraries
 C++ development
 X Window System
 Emacs
 Emacs with Xwindows
 Extra Documentation

 [[also select Networked workstation]]

 select ok and <enter>

31. Install Log screen:
 select ok and <enter>



32. Mouse type:
 select PS/2
 <enter>
 ( There is a problem here : the highlighted selection does not
tally with the hash mark)

33. Video Card:


 Matrox Millenium

34. Monitor

 Generic

35. Video memory
 selected  1MB  (set by accident; not sure)

36. No clockchip setting


37. resolutions

 800X600  8bit
 800X600  16bit
 640X400  24bit

38. Configure LAN
 select yes
 <enter>

39.
 Configure TCP/IP


 IP address : xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx
 Netmask    : 255.255.255.0
 default gateway: xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx
 primary nameserver: xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx

40. Configure Network
 domain name: xxx.xxx.xxx.edu
 host name: xxx.xxx.xxx.edu
 secondary name server xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx
 <enter>

41. Timezone
 set hardware clock to GMT
 select US/central
 <enter>

42. select printer
 no printer

43. root password


--------------------------------------------------------------------
44. Upgrade system: install bootloader. -> copies

 boot sda2:vmlinux.gz root =/dev/sda2


