>>>>> "JW" == John Walstra <walstra@cig.mot.com> writes:

    JW> And of course there is no LILO, which is causing my fears.  Do
    JW> I have to do anything to MILO when ever I recompile my kernel?
    JW> Does MILO only need to change when I upgrade my kernel (ei. to
    JW> 2.0.32).

Unlike LILO, MILO does not write any configuration information to the
hard disk, and since it is capable of reading ext2 file systems
directly, it does not need to know the starting location of the new
kernel.  All it needs to know is the path name and the file system
type.  You can type this in by hand at boot (which you should have
encountered already), or you can store this information in firmware
(either in ARC or in the MILO environment(?)).

Whenever you upgrade the kernel, just copy it over the old one.  Upon
reboot MILO will load whatever is in that file...

HTH?

