>>>>> "PT" == Paul Tomblin <ptomblin@xcski.com> writes:

    PT> I have an Alpha UDB.  How do I figure out how much video ram
    PT> is in the machine?  Do different TGAs have different amounts
    PT> of RAM or is it the same for all of them?  Also, I know the
    PT> FTP site for the X_TGA driver says it only supports 8
    PT> bitplanes - is this because the card only has 8 bit planes or
    PT> is there a prospect that some day I'll be able to get more
    PT> colours?

IIRC, the 21030 on the UDB was coupled to a Bt485 RAMDAC, which is
only capable of 8-bpp.  The total RAM size is 2MB.  This allows you to
do 1024x768 (with double-buffering), 1280x1024, and 1600x1200, all in
8-bpp mode.  The Z-buffer and stencil buffer is not available in this
configuration.  I believe this is called frame buffer option T8-02.

There are other versions of the TGA device that are capable of higher
color depths and have more memory, but I think those were separate PCI
expansion boards and aren't available from DEC any more (having been
replaced by the PowerStorm line, I think).

