I'm assuming you (correctly) made a MILO diskette from the milo.dd
image.  Now, to boot off the floppy drive from the SRM console, type
the command "boot dva0" (if you do a "show dev" you'll get a list of
all bootable devices on your system...dva0 should be one of them).
MILO should start right up.

Put in the Linux kernel disk, and continue with the MILO command "boot
fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1".

Detailed instructions of a Red Hat install onto a Multia are available
at <http://www.dcginc.com/linux.htm>.

(Alternatively, you can do a "set os_type NT" in SRM, then reboot.
ARC will come up by default at that time.)

