Thomas Hollunder wrote:
> 
> I finally managed to install 2.0.33 on our LX164 (RH4.2, 
> alpha-patches-2.0.32-0)
> 
> But when using gcc version 2.7.2.1 to compile anything that uses
> resource.h I get the following:
> 
> In file included from /usr/include/sys/resource.h:27,
>                  from mergemem.h:23,
>                  from mergemem.c:23:
[... deleted complaints of undefied limits ...]
> 
> Does anybody have a clue what the problem could be?
Yup. I had the very same (2.0.33/Redhat). resource.h includes
/usr/include/asm/resource.h, where a bunch of system-specific
Resource-Limits *should* be defined. Unfortunately, there are
only the limits for the Kernel (as in __KERNEL_RLIMIT_CPU), I
plainly copied the defs for the kernel, removed the __KERNEL_
prefix and voil`a. 
Maybe the compiler will then barf on a statement about 
RLIM_INFINITY somewhere else (a parse error IIRC). I just com-
mented out that one. It worked (and still works) for me, but as
usual, your mileage may vary.

regards,
Tobias

