>>>>> "PT" == Paul Tomblin <ptomblin@xcski.com> writes:

    PT> Is there a way to make it switch back to using the 10BaseT
    PT> port in these situations without rebooting?

The DE4X5 device has auto-sensing, so in theory, it should switch back
automatically.  However, I've had problems on my AlphaStation 200
getting it to switch back to 10baseT from 10base2.  Rather than
reboot, I just take the interface down and back up, e.g.:

	/sbin/ifconfig eth0 down
	/sbin/ifconfig eth0 up

The interface retains its configuration data (IP address, gateway,
netmask, etc.), but this will force the device driver to re-sense the
external connector.  WARNING: you *will* loose the ARP and RARP caches
as a result.

I haven't tried it ('cuz my network setup at home is very, very
strange), but I think you can set the connector type in firmware.
Boot the SRM console, and type 'show'.  Somewhere is listed something
like "esa0_auto_sense" or maybe "esa0_media_type".  It'll probably be
set to AUTO.  You can use the 'set' command to change that to TP or
BNC (whichever it is you use) I think permanently (so the driver will
disable autosense).  Like I said, I haven't tried it, but it's worth
checking out if you don't use the other media types.

