To my knowledge, there are only two Linux/Alpha distributions
available: RH5.0, and Gnu/Debian.  RH is a commercial product and
obviously works; I have it installed here.  However, initial installs
only work at the console in single-user mode.  Debian/Alpha is still in
development.  It does work.  I also have it installed here.  Debian is
my choice in the long run, but the initial install is not clean at the
moment (takes a bit of hacking).  Among the many benefits of Debian is
installing and upgrading via ethernet (which I do frequently on Intel
machines). 

> 
