S.T. Wong wrote:
> 
> Hi there,
> 
> When I install RH 5.0 on a XL266, everything seems okay until when I was
> prompted to insert the ramdisk.  Error message "Couldn't find valid ramdisk
> image starts at 0" (or something like that) was displayed.  The ramdisk was
> created with "standard" method (I tried both dd and rawrite).  I wonder what's
> wrong with it.
> 
> Would anyone please help ?
> 
> Thank you very much.
> Regards,
> ST Wong

When I had a similar situation for an EB164, I got boot and ram
disks from ftp.digital.com (binary ftp'd then dd'd to floppy), 
and used them with the milo disk dd'd from a Redhat 5.0 cd. No 
other combination that I tried of the six {Redhat, Digital} x 
{milo, boot, ram} disks worked. 

Also, you have to be careful about which disk is what, and the
documentation does not use unique names for each disk.  For an eb164,
you need

 milo disk, in "milo/images/eb164.img"
 kernel disk ==  boot disk, in "images/eb164.img"
 ram disk == root disk == supplemental disk, in "images/ramdisk.img"

IMHO we should call them milo, kernel, and ram disks only, and organize
them like 

 ramdisk
 eb164/boot.img
 eb164/kernel.img

John

