Walter H. Goodman (wgoodman@worldnet.att.net) wrote:
: My questions to this group are.... A) what video cards will FIT
: in the UDB box and B) of those that will fit and are still commercially
: available, which are supported through Linux and XFree86?

 Generally most S3 based cards (Trio64+, Virge) are small enough to
fit in the slot and will work. Bottom line: The card may be no longer
than 6.125" (155mm) and no taller than 4" (102mm) from the PCI slot.
A problem can be a BIOS emulation code in ARC console which is supposed
to initialize these beasties.  It is not likely to know anything about
new cards and manufacturers are not famous for following any standards.
But we tried S3 cards with UDB in the past and they did work.  YMMV.
Past ARC initialization anything which is supported by the current
XFree is supposed to work.  You may need to pick up a new milo from
ftp.redhat.com, its mirrors or gatekeeper.dec.com.

  Michal




