Hi, all.

I made a compatible and optimized dgemm.f routine for Alpha.  
This program is written in assembler and works on Linux/Alpha and
Digital UNIX.

My target is 21164 or 21164A.

21164PC, 21064 and 21066 will work fine, but will be slow.

   table 1. The ability of DGEMM routine(21164A 600MHz + 2MB L3 cache)
	   ---------------------------------------------
	   Matrix Sizes | N x N | N x T | T x N | T x T
	   -------------+-------+-------+-------+-------
	     200 x  200 |  800  |  761  |  761  |  761
	     400 x  400 |  761  |  771  |  748  |  744
	     600 x  600 |  764  |  756  |  743  |  735
	    1000 x 1000 |  766  |  749  |  750  |  746
	    1200 x 1200 |  759  |  756  |  745  |  736
	    1400 x 1400 |  759  |  758  |  745  |  740
	    1600 x 1600 |  750  |  742  |  729  |  727
	    2000 x 2000 |  752  |  758  |  734  |  737
	   ---------------------------------------------
                    note: There are maximal value for several times.

My routine shows about 750 to 760MFlops constantly with any
sizes( DEC's DXML shows 560 to 580MFlops on 1000x1000 matrix).

If you're interested in my routine, please see

ftp://ftp.eni.co.jp/.2/Linux-Alpha-JP/ftp.statabo.rim.or.jp/BLAS

The latest version is libdgemm-980413.tar.gz.  If you have any
suggestions or comments, please mail me.

Thanks,
  goto@statabo.rim.or.jp



