I have recently been going through a great deal of trouble attempting to assign
a different IRQ to my sound card on my XL300. Along the way I have gotten a
great deal of information from DEC about IRQs on the XL300. The system
configuration option of the AlphaBios gives a tremendous amount of read only
information on every device in the system including the values of all the PCI
registers for the PCI devices. This is a quick and easy way to discover things
like IRQs which are currently spoken for by existing devices.

DEC also sent me a list of the default IRQ assignments on a stock XL300 when it
leaves the factory.

 > >What I found for IRQ assignments for an ALPHA XL are as follows:
 > >
 > >
 > >IRQ # Source
 > >0 Timer/counter
 > >1 Keyboard
 > >2 Internal cascade of 8259
 > >3 Serial port 2 or ISA slot
 > >4 Serial port 1 or ISA slot
 > >5 Parallel port, PCI interrupt, or ISA slot
 > >6 Floppy controller or ISA slot
 > >7 Parallel port or ISA slot
 > >8 Reserved
 > >9 ISA slot
 > >10 ISA slot
 > >11 ISA slot
 > >12 Mouse or ISA slot
 > >13 Reserved
 > >14 ISA slot
 > >15 ISA slot
 > >
 > >
 > >This is from table C-2 of the Digital Alpha XL Family Users Guide
 > pn:
 > >EK-ALXLA-UG.C01


