> that the Multia will take only "True Parity, interleaved" SIMMs.  Is
> that what generic parity SIMMs are?  If I wanted to purchase memory
> from a third-party vendor (like PNY), what should I look for?

36bit, 72pins, 60/70ns simms is what you need.

Most generic simms are EDO/FastPage and 32/33bits
which won't work at all in your Multia.
 
