>>>>> "e" == ej  <ej@nwsports.com> writes:

    e> I do have a question with regard to firmware upgrades
    e> though. Is POST not updateable from the firmware upgrade or is
    e> the firmware update limited to FLASH areas only?

IIRC, the power-on self test is performed by code _burned_ into SROM,
not by the operating system consoles.  The consoles just initialize
the various necessary devices (console, disk, and ethernet) and load
the operating system and PAL (or at least that's all MILO seems to do,
and I'd guess SRM and ARC are not too different).  There's no way to
update the SROMs short of re-soldering new ones on to the
motherboard.

Are you still under warranty?  You may need to return the motherboard
to the vendor for service (or replacement).

HTH.

